{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And from</b> — And because many join themselves to him, he takes their counsel and advances with them and seizes a city. He devises a plan, and it does not come to pass now; therefore he said: it shall arise at another time."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The Hebrew reads יחשב מחשבת, literally 'he devises a plan'; I read this as Ibn Ezra's paraphrase of the verse's force, though the syntax is compressed and possibly elliptical."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:09.720412764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}